A||||23||88/2.8||Stereo Questions||||6||
Z||000000||88/2.8||11-07-2000||06:11 PM||||Does anyone know of a good stereo head unit/ sub that is medium-priced and looks good in a fiero? Doesn't nessesarily have to be stock. (I dont think i spelled that right)||||reg||6
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||11-07-2000||07:33 PM||||you can fit just about any head in there you want. stop by Best Buy and goto the sterio install bay they have all the adaptor kits... only cost like $20 for all the wiring and mounting plates. Altho you do have to get arround that chunk of metal in the back of the sterio hole. thing is a PITA, riveted into plastic, no way to get to it. I finally popped it out using two flat head screwdrivers and some elbow grease. But now I have my Sony CD player again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||11-07-2000||07:51 PM||||I have a Eclipse 5341R and a Eclipse .5 Din EQ. they fit great and look stock. I had to get a $45 instal kit to put them in. a Eclipse CD-player will run you from $275 to $1,700 for a DVD player w/ 5.1 Digital sound   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> or a good Clairon Pro audio Head unit will be from $200-700 just rember you WILL get what you pay for<P>Good name brands:<BR>Eclipse<BR>Clairon Pro-Audio<BR>Kenwoon Exelon<BR>Alpine<P>Names to stay away from:<BR>Pioneer<BR>Sony<BR>Awia<BR>Jensen<P>ANY CD headunit from Buest buy, Wall-mart, Sears or Curcit city  they are all mady buy a 3rd party and only cary the logo of Pioneer, Sony, Jvc, Alpine or Kenwood <p>[This message has been edited by Xtreme Fiero's (edited 11-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-08-2000||12:01 AM||||What's wrong with Pioneer or Sony?  I realize that Jensen is generally bottom of the line and apparently Aiwa is getting cheap, but the other 2 still have good reputations.<P>You might also consider JVC.  My cassette head unit is JVC.  Not top of the line, but good quality for a decent price.  It spent 4 months in a truck and still plays like new.||||reg||1
Z||000004||RiceCooker||11-08-2000||01:06 AM||||Yeah, JVC is great. I run a head unit with cassette hooked up to a 12 disc changer, and it's been running strong for 3 years.<P>Sony stinks IMHO. From what my friends have had (wasted their money on) you're only paying for the name, which as far as I'm concerned, only makes good speakers, TV's etc.<P>I've had Sony home mini systems too and they have always caused me grief. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||11-08-2000||01:10 AM||||I'm a big Sony fan, you can get a ot of features for the money.  I especially like the uni-knob controls that make it very easy to make adjustments without looking at the deck. Safety first! <BR>And if  like listening to the radio, my experience is that you don't find a better tuner then Pioneer. Alpine tuners SUCK! <BR>Kenwood is good stuff. I've had some very old-school Kenwoods that really took a licking and kept on ticking. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT Bastard||11-08-2000||08:05 AM||||I've had several pioneer deck, and they're and excellent unit for the money. My friend just went from a 40 by 4 Supertuner Pioneer to a newish Eclipse ESN and it sounded IDENTICAL.  He's running some nice speakers too(MBquartz, Polk audio, w/6in bass tube.) ||||reg||1
Z||000007||sparks||11-08-2000||09:11 AM||||Ok now I'm starting to wonder.  What's wrong with Aiwas????  I've got two for/in my vehicles, one I just bought for the Fiero and one in my Jeep.  Both are 40X4.  I don't have the one in my Fiero but I'm wondering if I should take it back and buy something else the way you guys talk around here.  The one in the Jeep sounds great, IMO.  But then I'm not wanting much more than something that sounds better than the stock system. I'm cheap and don't want to spend lots of money on stereo equipment with a 62 CJ-5 resto and a 73 Bug resto that're more important to me.  I've loved the Aiwa bookshelf systems that I own, based on them I bought my car stereos.<P>I almost took the Alpine out of the Bug for the Fiero, but getting it out is more trouble than it's worth so it'll stay.  But the Infinity Kappas in the Bug may make their way into my Fiero dash.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
Z||000008||1FST2M6||11-08-2000||09:16 AM||||My new toy!!! a 2000 Xtant 1001X... now just to build a new ensclouser...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   <A HREF="http://www.xtant.com" TARGET=_blank>www.xtant.com</A>   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstxtant.jpg">  <P>yeah thats me in the reflection! <P>jeff.. brad put a 6" tube in his fiero? hows it sound? BlackGt wants to do that but i keep tellin him no.. does it sound ok?<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||ThatRickGuy||11-08-2000||10:03 AM||||I've had no problems w/ the sony I've been using for the last year. It's a 4x45 w/1bit out put single CD player, I paid a whopping $125 for it. Hooked it up to a Rampage 4x500 watt amp, with a set of JVC 6x9s and a set of good 12"s, tweaked the cross over abit and it sounded wonderful, mids were a little weak, but I was going to pick up some 6" or 8" drivers to take car of that, but I sold the car befor I finished the sterio. so I pulled it all out and everything minus the head is sitting in the corner till I figure out how to fit it all back into the fiero. But anyway, the 1 bit outputs were crystal clear, and the amp held up fine with them. true the high output 4x45s are the greatest in the world, I've definately owned worse.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Xtreme Fiero's||11-08-2000||09:19 PM||||I curently have a Eclipse 5341r though 3 years old I have never needed to use the 4 year waranty once in 98 when I got it for $275 it was only entery level from Eclipse it did come with a remote ESN (theft lock) and 3 pair of 4v RCA outputs with Sub phase and level control. Once my whole stereo was stolen my eclipse with ESN was replaced & re-instaled for FREE!! in less than two weeks I will be instaling the Eclipse 55090 DVD/CD player with Dolby 5.1, DTS and voice controls this spring along with a Eclipse 39011 DSP, 5.1 digital & DTS decoder and a PPI PC21400 (if released to the public) IMO Eclipse is by far the best Brand of CD player folowed in order Mcintosh, Pro audio,Exelon and Alpine<P>the problem with Pioneer, Kenwood JVC and Clairon is that they all have a "Cheap" line and a "Pricey" lineup (Exelon, Pro Audio & Premier) thier regular cd players ar for the most part poor and thier "better" models are just upgraded botom end peices. They also base all of thier on Peak #'s like car HP think of your Awia cd player like a twin turbo 1.5 Civic shure it's got 4500HP At 7,000 RPM but only 900 elsewhere. like the SONY MDX-C800REC thier new top of the line MD player/ recorder in big yellow print it says "45W X 4"as tested buy car stereo review (oct/nov 2000) 45 X 4 realy means 45 X 4 @ 1,000 Hz and full distortion and only 21.5 X 4 at 1% THD (a human ear can pickup .80 Total Harmonic Distortion and above) and 1,000 Hz. You can see the problem.<P>I just wrote all this and forgot what I was getting at. but you WILL get what you pay for and 45 X 4 is only 45W X 4 if you turn it ALL the way up.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Seanh||11-08-2000||10:57 PM||||I hate to go against most here, but... In my experience, I think the cheapest Pioneers are better then some of the more expensive and "higher quality" headunits. I think that Premier (advanced Pioneer line) is one of the best brands out there, if not the best. Kenwood are also very good units. I have honestly had nothing but trouble with alot of the JVC's I have had. I dont like them. From my experience, heres what I would say:<BR><B>High end, quality brands</B><BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Premier<BR><LI>Kenwood<BR><LI>Sony (XES is so awesome)<BR><LI>Panisonic (Sorry about that one, but they are good)<BR><LI>Clairon<BR></UL><P><B>Good for normal everyday listeners</B><BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Pioneer<BR><LI>Alpine<BR><LI>Aiwa<BR><LI>Blaupunkt<BR><LI>Rockford Fosgate<BR><LI>JVC (more expensive models)<BR></UL><P><B>Bargain Brands</B><BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Jensen<BR><LI>Sanyo (Im not a fan of them at all)<BR><LI>JVC (Cheaper models)<BR></UL><P>Keep in mind this is only on headunits, when it comes to other accessories, its a whole new ball game.<BR>Just because you can find a certain brand (Pioneer and Sony to be specific) at places like Wal-Mart doesnt mean that they are crap. Usally places like that only carry the lower end models because that is what people are looking for when they go to Wal-Mart to get car stereos, likewise you wouldnt come to a stereo shop to get dishwashing soap.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">    <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula||11-09-2000||10:43 AM||||I have a higher up Alpine and the tuner DOES suck........but the cd quality is excellent.<P>I had a Jensen deck that distorted a lot when I turned it up.  but the alpine doesnt distort until a looooooooot later.<P>And I have an aiwa home stereo that is kick a$$.  I've always considered aiwa to be top of the line.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FormulaSignature2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||88/2.8||11-09-2000||10:48 AM||||Heeeyyy, nice formula, ive got one just like it. I like what you did with the red on the bottom. ||||reg||14
Z||000014||88/2.8||11-09-2000||11:12 AM||||Yes! I think i will go with kenwood.||||reg||1
Z||000015||3400Fiero||11-09-2000||04:18 PM||||I have a Clarion head unit (cassette and tuner + CD changer controller) and 6 CD changer under the glove box.  I am really happy with Clarion.  I think they have one of the best tuners on the market, and the CD and cassette deck quality are excellent.  I have replaced the front 4x10s with Kickers and the rear 4x6s with Hollywood speakers.  I am getting set to put 2 8in subs behind the seats, powered by an MTX Blue Thunder amp.  Can't wait to get it all put together!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000016||Tom88gt||11-10-2000||10:36 AM||||I've had more problems with Sony CD players (car changer, LD/CD player, discman) than all other brands combined.  I wont buy a Sony unless no one else makes a particluar device/design I need.  I had a lot of problems with a high end Sanyo model too (replaced once, both failed) but once sent back to the service center and repaired it has worked great.  A Jensen I had didn't fare well either.  Now I stick with name brands but I still shop mainly buy price and features needed for my particular system plan.<P>Many have had great luck with Sony but not me (maybe I'm jinxed).<P>Get a Crutchfield catalog.  Not great prices but fair.  The best customer service I've ever come across.  And they give you FREE install kits and wiring harnesses (worth about $20) that make their prices very competetive.||||reg||13
Z||000017||Philphine||11-10-2000||11:30 AM||||if you made me recommend a brand for some one else i'd always pick pioneer. i have other brands but pioneer is so common anybody and their grandma is going to sell it, fix it,or install it. eclipse almost borders on being a boutique name. you can't argue about it's quality but if you're not in a good sized city or near a higherend shop you could end up with a piece thats hard to get serviced. you could argue that it's quality will eliminate that need but why take that chance as a novice.<P>i like fooling with car stereo but make no expert claims. right now i have either installed or around the house 2 pioneer heads, 2 jvc, a denon, a clarion and an alpine (yes, i'm a junk monger). all have good points and bad so i would make no judgement brandwise, but if you have to ask for recommendations i would stick with a common brand to start and go for the exotic when you've picked up more background.||||reg||1
Z||000018||1FST2M6||11-10-2000||11:52 AM||||i had an Alpine i tried to GIVE to GT Bastard and even he wouldn't take it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'm big in to Sony. I had a CDX C910 and now a C-90 and have never had any problem with them.. the Kenwood KDC-7009 (flip face) that my girlfriend has, has been returned 3 times for service (the face sticks closed or open and ticks somthing awful! the Execelon series stuff seem nice...i guess we just got a Lemon. The Aiwa with the center channel mounted to the radio is pretty sweet! there is on ein the NOPI Focus ( <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  ) its a gimic but still cool. i don't know anything about its build quality though. ||||reg||1
Z||000019||Smith 85 2M4||11-10-2000||05:53 PM||||I have had numerous Sony's, everything from the old pull-out tape decks and cd players to a detachable face CD player.  The pull outs were very reliable, but I've had nothing but problems with the detachable face CD in my Fiero.  The buttons are falling off and only half of the LCD lights up.  What a piece of dung! I have one of those oversized Pioneer CD players for GM/Chryler in my pickup; it has been great!  It fits nice and flush in the dash with no modifications to the vehicle.  (I really should put it in the Fiero)  I would recommend an oversized Pioneer. They have a lot of features for the money ($250-300) and more amp power than most others, IMHO.<P>------------------<BR>Smith 85 2M4||||reg||7
Z||000020||Bugsy||11-14-2000||09:19 AM||||I just bought an Aiwa CDC-MP3 head unit, I bought it for its cd capabilities, reads cd's , cdr's, cdrw's AND MP3's....it has the little remote that clamps to the steering wheel, 2 sets of rca outs, 45x4, and of course removable face for $299. the only other option that could decode mp3 files was a Kenwood eXcelon z919...basically the same options and the same power output it has 3 sets of rca outs, but it was $649.95...so i settled for the Aiwa and because i'm not really that impressed with the quality, and longevity of the Aiwa brand...i bought a 4 year service contract...if they can't fix it, they'll replace it...but i'm starting to have second thoughts after what i've read in this thread   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin<p>[This message has been edited by Bugsy (edited 11-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||Oreif||11-14-2000||10:10 AM||||I have had Kenwood, Alpine, Sony, Pioneer, and blaupunkt over the many years. The only unit I did not like was the Sony. It sounded nice but broke easily (reliability was poor)<BR>As for stereo output All the above use the same exact driver circuit for the low level outputs. Which is what most "stereophiles" use since they use amps and crossovers. We even had a stereo in a car that had Alphasonic and Pioneer amps, Boston Acqustic speakers, and was driven by a Kraco $19 AM/FM/cassette player bought at Kmart on sale! It sounded as nice as any other stereo.  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||fiero87||11-14-2000||11:49 AM||||I work for circuit city on the weekends and have had some first hand experiance with all different brands.  Generally anything that is Kenwood, or Alpine is what we reccomend.  Pioneer is alright too.  Just stay away from any off brands (profile, Koss..etc)  I personally have had a sony for over a year and half and had no problems, but they guys in the roadshop call them "six month sony's"  Apparently they break is exacly 6 months.  lol  I do have an ES unit, maybe thats why i don't have any problems.  <BR>Tim||||reg||1
Z||000023||Hawk||11-14-2000||12:14 PM||||Has anybody considered the square units out of late model GM trucks? I converted my other car to that and it works great, good power and sound and it think it would fit the whole perfectly.||||reg||1
